comments.content:
Stale-ref race on unmount: `guidanceRef.current` is updated in this post-render effect, but the unmount cleanup at the top of the card persists whatever is currently in the ref. If the user types and the component unmounts (or re-mounts via section toggle teardown) between render and this effect running, the cleanup will write the *previous* value to storage — silently losing the last edit. Update the ref synchronously in the `onChange` handler instead, and drop this effect:

```tsx
onChange={(e) => {
  const v = e.target.value;
  guidanceRef.current = v; // sync, not in useEffect
  setGuidance(v);
  setGuidanceSaved(false);
}}
```

This also removes the dependency on the ref-update effect racing with React's commit phase.

