comments.content:
listen() cleanup has two latent issues: (1) if the promise rejects (Tauri IPC failure) the rejection is silently dropped; (2) if the component unmounts before `listen()` resolves, the listener can still be registered and fire `setShowTasks` on an unmounted component after teardown. Idiomatic Tauri pattern:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  let cancelled = false;
  let unlisten: UnlistenFn | undefined;
  listen<unknown>(WORKFLOW_VISIBILITY_EVENT, () => {
    if (!cancelled) setShowTasks(getShowWorkflowTasks());
  })
    .then((f) => {
      if (cancelled) f();
      else unlisten = f;
    })
    .catch((e) => console.error("workflow visibility listener:", e));
  return () => {
    cancelled = true;
    unlisten?.();
  };
}, []);
```

Also worth importing `type UnlistenFn` from `@tauri-apps/api/event` for the typed handle.

